{
  "title": "15: al-Hijr الحجر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالۤرٰ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ وَقُرْاٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(1)\nAR-RAA TILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE WAQURAAANIN MOBEEN.\nA. L. R. These are the Ayats of Revelation, of a Qur'an that makes things clear. \nرُبَمَا يَوَدُّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْ كَانُوْا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(2)\nRUBAMAA YAWADDO LAZEENA KAFAROO LAW KAANOO MUSLEMEEN.\nAgain and again will those who disbelieve, wish that they had bowed (to Allah's will) in Islam. \nذَرْهُمْ يَاْكُلُوْا وَيَتَمَتَّعُوْا وَيُلْهِهِمُ الْاَمَلُ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(3)\nZARHUM YAAKULOOA WAYATAMATTAU’OOA WAYULHEHEMU AL-AAMALU FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nLeave them alone, to enjoy (the good things of this life) and to please themselves: let (false) hope amuse them: soon will knowledge (undeceive them). \nوَمَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا وَلَهَا كِتَابٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌ‏(4)\nWA MAA AHLAKNAL MIN QARYATINW ILLAA WA LAHAA KETAABUN MMAA’LOOMUN.\nNever did We destroy a population that had not a term decreed and assigned beforehand. \nمَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ‏(5)\nMAA TASBEQU MIN UMMATIN AAJALAHAA WA MAA YASTAAKHEROONA.\nNeither can a people anticipate its term, nor delay it. \nوَ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِىْ نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ اِنَّكَ لَمَجْنُوْنٌؕ‏(6)\nWA QAALOO YAA AYYOHAL LAZEE NUZZELA A’LAYHE AZ-ZEKRU INNAKA LAMAJNOONUN.\nThey say: “O thou to whom the Message is being revealed! truly thou art mad (or possessed)! \nلَوْ مَا تَاْتِيْنَا بِالْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(7)\nLAW MAA TAATEENAA BIL-MALAAEKATE IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\n“Why bringest thou not angels to us if it be that thou hast the Truth?” \nمَا نُنَزِّلُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةَ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَمَا كَانُوْۤا اِذًا مُّنْظَرِيْنَ‏(8)\nMAA NUNAZZELU AL-MALAAEKATA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA MAA KAANOO EZAL MMUNZAREENA.\nWe send not the angels down except for just cause: if they came (to the ungodly), behold! no respite would they have! \nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَحٰفِظُوْنَ‏(9)\nINNAA NAHNO NAZZALNAA KHASEYAR WA INNAA LAHU LAHAAFEZOONA.\nWe have, without doubt, sent down the Message; and We will assuredly guard it (from corruption). \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ فِىْ شِيَعِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA FEE SHEEE’E AWWALEEN.\nWe did send messengers before thee amongst the religious sects of old: \nوَمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(11)\nWA MAA YAATEEHIM MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nBut never came a messenger to them but they mocked him. \nكَذٰلِكَ نَسْلُكُهٗ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(12)\nKAZAALEKA NASLUKUH FEE QOLOOBIL MUJREMEEN.\nEven so do we let it creep into the hearts of the sinners - \nلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖۚ وَقَدْ خَلَتْ سُنَّةُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(13)\nLAA YOAMENOONA BEHI WA QAD KHALAT SUNNATU AWWALEEN.\nThat they should not believe in the (Message); but the ways of the ancients have passed away. \nوَلَوْ فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ فَظَلُّوْا فِيْهِ يَعْرُجُوْنَۙ‏(14)\nWA LAW FATAHNA A’LAYHIM BAABAN MENAL SAMAAA-E FAZALLOOA FEEHE YAA’RUJOONA.\nEven if We opened out to them a gate from heaven, and they were to continue (all day) ascending therein, \nلَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَا سُكِّرَتْ اَبْصَارُنَا بَلْ نَحْنُ قَوْمٌ مَّسْحُوْرُوْنَ‏(15)\nLAQAALOOA INNAMAA SUKKERAT AABSAARUNAA BAL NAHNO QAWMUN MMASHOOROONA.\nThey would only say: “Our eyes have been intoxicated: Nay, we have been bewitched by sorcery.” \nوَلَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا فِى السَّمَآءِ بُرُوْجًا وَّزَيَّنّٰهَا لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَۙ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD JA-A’LNAA FIL SAMAAA-E BUROOJAN WWAZAYNNAAHAA LELNNAAZEREENA.\nIt is We Who have set out the zodiacal signs in the heavens, and made them fair-seeming to (all) beholders; \nوَحَفِظْنٰهَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْطٰنٍ رَّجِيْمٍۙ‏(17)\nWAHAFEZNAAHAA MIN KULLE SHAYTAANIR RAJEEMIN.\nAnd (moreover) We have guarded them from every cursed devil: \nاِلَّا مَنِ اسْتَرَقَ السَّمْعَ فَاَ تْبَعَهٗ شِهَابٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(18)\nILLAA MANIS ASTARAQA JA-A’LA FA-ALQEEHE TBAA’AH SHEHAABUN MOBEEN.\nBut any that gains a hearing by stealth, is pursued by a flaming fire, bright (to see). \nوَالْاَرْضَ مَدَدْنٰهَا وَاَلْقَيْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مَّوْزُوْنٍ‏(19)\nWAL ARZA MADADNAAHAA WAALQAYNAA FEEHAA JA-A’LA WAANBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE SHAY-IN MMAWZOONIN.\nAnd the earth We have spread out (like a carpet); set thereon mountains firm and immovable; and produced therein all kinds of things in due balance. \nوَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَعَايِشَ وَمَنْ لَّسْتُمْ لَهٗ بِرٰزِقِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA JA-A’LNAA LAKUM FEEHAA MAA’AAYESHA WA MAN LLASTUM LAHU BERAAZEQEENA.\nAnd We have provided therein means of subsistence, for you and for those for whose sustenance ye are not responsible. \nوَاِنْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا عِنْدَنَا خَزَآئِنُهٗ وَمَا نُنَزِّلُهٗۤ اِلَّا بِقَدَرٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍ‏(21)\nWA MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA E’ENDANAA KHAZAAENUH WA MAA NUNAZZELUH ILLAA BEQADARIN MA’LOOM.\nAnd there is not a thing but its (sources and) treasures (inexhaustible) are with Us; but We only send down thereof in due and ascertainable measures. \nوَاَرْسَلْنَا الرِّيٰحَ لَوَاقِحَ فَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَسْقَيْنٰكُمُوْهُۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ لَهٗ بِخٰزِنِيْنَ‏(22)\nWA ARSALNAA REYAAHA LAWAAQEHA FA-ANZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FAASQAYNAAKUMOOHU WA MAA ANTUM LAHU BEKHAAZENEENA.\nAnd We send the fecundating winds, then cause the rain to descend from the sky, therewith providing you with water (in abundance), though ye are not the guardians of its stores. \nوَ اِنَّا لَنَحْنُ نُحْىٖ وَنُمِيْتُ وَنَحْنُ الْوٰرِثُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA INNAA LANAHNU NUHAA WANUMEETU WA NAHNO AL-WAARESOONA.\nAnd verily, it is We Who give life, and Who give death: it is We Who remain inheritors (after all else passes away). \nوَلَقَدْ عَلِمْنَا الْمُسْتَقْدِمِيْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْنَا الْمُسْتَاْخِرِيْنَ‏(24)\nWA LAQAD A’LIMNAA AL-MUSTAQDEMEENA MINKUM WA LAQAD A’LIMNAA AL-MUSTAAKHEREENA.\nTo Us are known those of you who hasten forward, and those who lag behind. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَحْشُرُهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(25)\nWA INNA RABBAKA HOWA YAHSHURUHUM INNAHU HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nAssuredly it is thy Lord Who will gather them together: for He is perfect in Wisdom and Knowledge. \nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَاٍ مَّسْنُوْنٍۚ‏(26)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA MIN SALSAALIN MIN HAMAA MMASNOONIN.\nWe created man from sounding clay, from mud moulded into shape; \nوَالْجَآنَّ خَلَقْنٰهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ مِنْ نَّارِ السَّمُوْمِ‏(27)\nWA JAAAN-NA KHALAQNAAHO MIN QABLO MIN NNAARE AS-SAMOOME.\nAnd the Jinn race, We had created before, from the fire of a scorching wind. \nوَاِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنِّىْ خَالِقٌۢ بَشَرًا مِّنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَاٍ مَّسْنُوْنٍ‏(28)\nWA IZ QAALA RABBOKA LIL-MALAAEKATE INNEE KHAALEQUN BASHARAN MIN SALSAALIN MIN HAMAA MMASNOONIN.\nBehold! thy Lord said to the angels: “I am about to create man, from sounding clay from mud moulded into shape; \nفَاِذَا سَوَّيْتُهٗ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِىْ فَقَعُوْا لَهٗ سٰجِدِيْنَ‏(29)\nFA-EZAA SAWYTUH WANAFAKHTU FEEHE MIN RROOHEAA FAQAU’OOA LAHU SAAJEDEENA.\n“When I have fashioned him (in due proportion) and breathed into him of My spirit, fall ye down in obeisance unto him.” \nفَسَجَدَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ كُلُّهُمْ اَجْمَعُوْنَۙ‏(30)\nFASAJADA AL-MALAAEKATU KULLUHUM AAJMAU’OONA.\nSo the angels prostrated themselves, all of them together: \nاِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اَبٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ مَعَ السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(31)\nILLAA IBLEES AABAAA AN YAKOONA LAAHA AS-SAAJEDEENA.\nNot so Iblis: he refused to be among those who prostrated themselves. \nقَالَ يٰۤاِبْلِيْسُ مَا لَكَ اَلَّا تَكُوْنَ مَعَ السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALA YAABLEESU MAA LAKA ALLAA TAKOONA LAAHA AS-SAAJEDEENA.\n(Allah) said: “O Iblis! what is your reason for not being among those who prostrated themselves?” \nقَالَ لَمْ اَكُنْ لِّاَسْجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهٗ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَاٍ مَّسْنُوْنٍ‏(33)\nQAALA LAM AAKUN LEAASJUDA LEBASHARIN KHALAQTAH MIN SALSAALIN MIN HAMAA MMASNOONIN.\n(Iblis) said: “I am not one to prostrate myself to man, whom Thou didst create from sounding clay, from mud moulded into shape.” \nقَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَاِنَّكَ رَجِيْمٌۙ‏(34)\nQAALA FAKHRUJ MINHAA FA-INNAKA RAJEEMUN.\n(Allah) said: “Then get thee out from here; for thou art rejected, accursed. \nوَّاِنَّ عَلَيْكَ اللَّعْنَةَ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ‏(35)\nWWAANNA A’LAYKA AL-LAA’NATA ELAA YAWMIL DEENE.\n“And the curse shall be on thee till the day of Judgment.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ فَاَنْظِرْنِىْۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(36)\nQAALA RABBE FAANZERNEAA ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\n(Iblis) said: “O my Lord! give me then respite till the Day the (dead) are raised.” \nقَالَ فَاِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِيْنَۙ‏(37)\nQAALA FA-INNAKA MENAL AL-MUNZAREENA.\n(Allah) said: “Respite is granted thee \nاِلٰى يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُوْمِ‏(38)\nELAA YAWMIL AL-WAQTE AL-MAA’LOOME.\n“Till the Day of the Time appointed.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَاۤ اَغْوَيْتَنِىْ لَاُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَاُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(39)\nQAALA RABBE BEMAA AAGHWAYTANEAA LAAZAYNANNA LAHUM FIL ARZE WALAAGHWEENNAHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\n(Iblis) said: “O my Lord! because Thou hast put me in the wrong, I will make (wrong) fair-seeming to them on the earth, and I will put them all in the wrong, \nاِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(40)\nILLAA E’EBAADAKA MENHUMU AL-MUKHLASEENA.\n“Except Thy servants among them, sincere and purified (by Thy Grace).” \nقَالَ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ عَلَىَّ مُسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(41)\nQAALA HAAZAA SERAATUM A’LAYYA MUSTAQEEMUN.\n(Allah) said: “This (way of My sincere servants) is indeed a way that leads straight to Me. \nاِنَّ عِبَادِىْ لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنٌ اِلَّا مَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْغٰوِيْنَ‏(42)\nINNAL E’BAADEE LAYSA LAKA A’LAYHIM SULTAANUN ILLAA MANIS ATTABAA’AKA MENAL AL-GHAAWEENA.\n“For over My servants no authority shalt thou have, except such as put themselves in the wrong and follow thee.” \nوَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمَوْعِدُهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(43)\nWA INNA JAHANNAMA LAMAWE’EDUHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nAnd verily, Hell is the promised abode for them all! \nلَهَا سَبْعَةُ اَبْوَابٍؕ لِكُلِّ بَابٍ مِّنْهُمْ جُزْءٌ مَّقْسُوْمٌ‏(44)\nLAHAA SABA’ATU AABWAABIN LEKULLIM BAABIN MINHUM JUZUN MMAQSOOMUN.\nTo it are seven gates: for each of those gates is a (special) class (of sinners) assigned. \nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍؕ‏(45)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE JANNAATIN WWAU’UYOONIN.\nThe righteous (will be) amid gardens and fountains (of clear-flowing water). \nاُدْخُلُوْهَا بِسَلٰمٍ اٰمِنِيْنَ‏(46)\nAUDKHULOOHAA BESALAAMIN AAMENEENA.\n(Their greeting will be): “Enter ye here in peace and security.” \nوَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ مِّنْ غِلٍّ اِخْوَانًا عَلٰى سُرُرٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(47)\nWA NAZA’NAA MAA FEE SODOOREHIM MIN GHELLIN AEKHWAANAN A’LAA SORORIM MOTAQAABELEENA.\nAnd We shall remove from their hearts any lurking sense of injury: (they will be) brothers (joyfully) facing each other on thrones (of dignity). \nلَا يَمَسُّهُمْ فِيْهَا نَصَبٌ وَّمَا هُمْ مِّنْهَا بِمُخْرَجِيْنَ‏(48)\nLAA YAMASSUHUM FEEHAA NASABUN WA MAA HUM MINHAA BEMUKHRAJEENA.\nThere no sense of fatigue shall touch them, nor shall they (ever) be asked to leave. \nنَبِّئْ عِبَادِىْۤ اَنِّىْۤ اَنَا الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُۙ‏(49)\nNABBE E’BAADEE AANNEAA ANAA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nTell My servants that I am indeed the Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful; \nوَاَنَّ عَذَابِىْ هُوَ الْعَذَابُ الْاَلِيْمُ‏(50)\nWA ANNAL A’AZAABEAA HOWA A’ZAABO AL-AALEEMU.\nAnd that My Penalty will be indeed the most grievous Penalty. \nوَنَبِّئْهُمْ عَنْ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَۘ‏(51)\nWANABBEHUM A’N ZAYFE IBRAAHEEMA.\nTell them about the guests of Abraham. \nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًاؕ قَالَ اِنَّا مِنْكُمْ وَجِلُوْنَ‏(52)\nIZ DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FA-QAALOO SALAAMAN QAALA INNAA MINKUM WAJELOONA.\nWhen they entered his presence and said, “Peace!” He said, “We feel afraid of you!” \nقَالُوْا لَا تَوْجَلْ اِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(53)\nQAALOO LAA TAWJAL INNAA NUBASSHERUKA BEGHULAAMIN A’LEEM.\nThey said: “Fear not! We give thee glad tidings of a son endowed with wisdom.” \nقَالَ اَبَشَّرْتُمُوْنِىْ عَلٰٓى اَنْ مَّسَّنِىَ الْكِبَرُ فَبِمَ تُبَشِّرُوْنَ‏(54)\nQAALA AABASSHARTUMOONEAA A’LAA AN MMASSANEAAA KEBARO FA BEMA TUBASSHEROONA.\nHe said: “Do ye give me glad tidings that old age has seized me? Of what, then, is your good news?” \nقَالُوْا بَشَّرْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْقٰنِطِيْنَ‏(55)\nQAALOO BASSHARNAAKA BIL-HAQQE FALAA TAKUN MENAL AL-QAANETEENA.\nThey said: “We give thee glad tidings in truth: be not then in despair!” \nقَالَ وَمَنْ يَّقْنَطُ مِنْ رَّحْمَةِ رَبِّهٖۤ اِلَّا الضَّآلُّوْنَ‏(56)\nQAALA WA MAN YYAQNATU MIN RRAHMATE RABBEHI ILLAA ZAALLOONAL.\nHe said: “And who despairs of the mercy of his Lord, but such as go astray?” \nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(57)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBUKUM AYYOHAL MURSALOON.\nAbraham said: “What then is the business on which ye (have come), O ye messengers (of Allah)?” \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(58)\nQAALOO INNAA AURSELNAA ELAA QAWMIN MMUJREMEENA.\nThey said: “We have been sent to a people (deep) in sin, \nاِلَّاۤ اٰلَ لُوْطٍؕ اِنَّا لَمُنَجُّوْهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(59)\nILLAA AALA LOOTIN INNAA LAMUNAJJOOHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\n“Excepting the adherents of Lut: them we are certainly (charged) to save (from harm), All - \nاِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ قَدَّرْنَاۤ ۙ اِنَّهَا لَمِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(60)\nILLAA RA-ATAHU QADDARNAA INNAHAA LAMENAS GHAABEREEN.\n“Except his wife, who, We have ascertained, will be among those who will lag behind.” \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اٰلَ لُوْطِ ۨالْمُرْسَلُوْنَۙ‏(61)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AALA LOOTE MURSALOON.\nAt length when the messengers arrived among the adherents of Lut, \nقَالَ اِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‏(62)\nQAALA INNAKUM QAWMUN MMUNKAROONA.\nHe said: “Ye appear to be uncommon folk.” \nقَالُوْا بَلْ جِئْنٰكَ بِمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(63)\nQAALOO BAL JENAAKA BEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAMTAROONA.\nThey said: “Yea, we have come to thee to accomplish that of which they doubt. \nوَ اَتَيْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA AATAYNAAKA BIL-HAQQE WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\n“We have brought to thee that which is inevitably due, and assuredly we tell the truth. \nفَاَسْرِ بِاَهْلِكَ بِقِطْعٍ مِّنَ الَّيْلِ وَاتَّبِعْ اَدْبَارَهُمْ وَلَا يَلْتَفِتْ مِنْكُمْ اَحَدٌ وَّامْضُوْا حَيْثُ تُؤْمَرُوْنَ‏(65)\nFA-ASRE BEAAHLEKA BEQETA’IN MENAL LAYLE WAATTABEA’ AADBAARAHUM WA LAA YALTAFET MINKUM AHAD WWAAMZOOA HAYSO TOAMAROON.\n“Then travel by night with thy household, when a portion of the night (yet remains), and do thou bring up the rear: let no one amongst you look back, but pass on whither ye are ordered.” \nوَقَضَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ ذٰ لِكَ الْاَمْرَ اَنَّ دَابِرَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مَقْطُوْعٌ مُّصْبِحِيْنَ‏(66)\nWA QAZAYNAA ELAYHE ZAA LEKA AMRA ANNAL DAABERA HAAOOLAAA-E MAQTOOA’UN MMUSBEHEENA.\nAnd We made known this decree to him, that the last remnants of those (sinners) should be cut off by the morning. \nوَجَآءَ اَهْلُ الْمَدِيْنَةِ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA JAAA-A AAHLU MADEENATE YASTABSHEROON.\nThe inhabitants of the city came in (mad) joy (at news of the young men). \nقَالَ اِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ضَيْفِىْ فَلَا تَفْضَحُوْنِۙ‏(68)\nQAALA INNAL HAAOOLAAA-E ZAYFEAA FALAA TAFZAHOONE.\nLut said: “These are my guests: disgrace me not: \nوَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُخْزُوْنِ‏(69)\nWAT TAQUL LAAHA WA LAA TUKHZOONE.\n“But fear Allah, and shame me not.” \nقَالُوْۤا اَوَلَمْ نَنْهَكَ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(70)\nQAALOO AWALAM NANHAKA A’NIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThey said: “Did we not forbid thee (to speak) for all and sundry?” \nقَالَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ بَنٰتِىْۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فٰعِلِيْنَؕ‏(71)\nQAALA HAAOOLAAA-E BANAATEAA IN KUNTUM FAAE’ELEENA.\nHe said: “There are my daughters (to marry), if ye must act (so).” \nلَعَمْرُكَ اِنَّهُمْ لَفِىْ سَكْرَتِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(72)\nLAA’AMRUKA INNAHUM LAFEE SAKRATEHEM YA’MAHOON.\nVerily, by thy life (O Prophet), in their wild intoxication, they wander in distraction, to and fro. \nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُشْرِقِيْنَۙ‏(73)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUR AS-SAYHATU MUSHREQEENA.\nBut the (mighty) Blast overtook them before morning, \nفَجَعَلْنَا عَالِيَهَا سَافِلَهَا وَ اَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ سِجِّيْلٍؕ‏(74)\nFA JA-A’LNAA A’AALEEHAA SAAFELAHAA WA AAMTARNAA A’LAYHIM HEJAARATAN MIN SEJJEELIN.\nAnd We turned (the cities) upside down, and rained down on them brimstones hard as baked clay. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّلْمُتَوَسِّمِيْنَ‏(75)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LLELMUTAWASSEMEENA.\nBehold! in this are Signs for those who by tokens do understand. \nوَاِنَّهَا لَبِسَبِيْلٍ مُّقِيْمٍ‏(76)\nINNAHAA LABESABEELIN MMUQEEMIN.\nAnd the (cities were) right on the high-road. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(77)\nINNAL FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LLELMUMENEENA.\nBehold! in this is a sign for those who believed. \nوَاِنْ كَانَ اَصْحٰبُ الْاَيْكَةِ لَظٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(78)\nWA KAANA ASHAABUN AL-AAYKATE LAZAALEMEENA.\nAnd the Companions of the Wood were also wrong-doers; \nفَانتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْۘ وَاِنَّهُمَا لَبِاِمَامٍ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(79)\nFAANTAQAMNAA MINHUM WAANNAHUMAA LABEAEMAAMIN MMUBEENIN.\nSo We exacted retribution from them. They were both on an open highway, plain to see. \nوَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ اَصْحٰبُ الْحِجْرِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۙ‏(80)\nWA LAQAD KAZZABA ASHAABUN AL-HEJRE MURSALEEN.\nThe Companions of the Rocky Tract also rejected the messengers: \nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ اٰيٰتِنَا فَكَانُوْا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِيْنَۙ‏(81)\nWA AATAYNAAHUM AAYAATENAA FA KAANOO A’NHAA MOA’REZEEN.\nWe sent them Our Signs, but they persisted in turning away from them. \nوَكَانُوْا يَنْحِتُوْنَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا اٰمِنِيْنَ‏(82)\nWA KAANOO YANHETOONA MENAL JEBAALE BUYOOTAN AAMENEENA.\nOut of the mountains did they hew (their) edifices, (feeling themselves) secure. \nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُصْبِحِيْنَۙ‏(83)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUR AS-SAYHATU MUSBEHEENA.\nBut the (mighty) Blast seized them of a morning, \nفَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَؕ‏(84)\nFAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOONA.\nAnd of no avail to them was all that they did (with such art and care)! \nوَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَاۤ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَاٰتِيَةٌ فَاصْفَحِ الصَّفْحَ الْجَمِيْلَ‏(85)\nWA MAA KHALAQNAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA INNA SAA-A’TA LAATEETUN FAASFAHE AS-SAFHA AL-JAMEELA.\nWe created not the heavens, the earth, and all between them, but for just ends. And the Hour is surely coming (when this will be manifest). So overlook (any human faults) with gracious forgiveness. \nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْخَلّٰقُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(86)\nINNAL RABBAKA HOWA KHALLAAQUL A’LEEM.\nFor verily it is thy Lord who is the Master-Creator, knowing all things. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنٰكَ سَبْعًا مِّنَ الْمَثَانِىْ وَالْقُرْاٰنَ الْعَظِيْمَ‏(87)\nWA LAQAD AAATAYNAAKA SAB-A’N MENAL AL-MASAANEAA WA QURAANA AL-A’AZEEMA.\nAnd We have bestowed upon thee the Seven Oft-repeated (verses) and the Grand Qur'an. \nلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ اِلٰى مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْهُمْ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(88)\nLAA TAMUDDANNA A’AYNAYKA ELAA MAA MATTAA’NAA BEHI AZWAAJANW MINHUM WA LAA TAHZAN A’LAYHIM WAAKHFEZ JANAAHAKA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nStrain not thine eyes. (Wistfully) at what We have bestowed on certain classes of them, nor grieve over them: but lower thy wing (in gentleness) to the believers. \nوَقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اَنَا النَّذِيْرُ الْمُبِيْنُۚ‏(89)\nWA QUL INNEE ANAA AN-NAZEERU MOBEEN.\nAnd say: “I am indeed he that warneth openly and without ambiguity,”- \nكَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَى الْمُقْتَسِمِيْنَۙ‏(90)\nKAMAA ANZALNAA A’LAL AL-MUQTASEMEENA.\n(Of just such wrath) as We sent down on those who divided (Scripture into arbitrary parts), \nالَّذِيْنَ جَعَلُوا الْقُرْاٰنَ عِضِيْنَ‏(91)\nLAZEENA JAA’ALOOA QURAANA E’EZEENA.\n(So also on such) as have made Qur'an into shreds (as they please). \nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَسْئَلَنَّهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(92)\nFAWARABBEKA LANASALANNAHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nTherefore, by the Lord, We will, of a surety, call them to account, \nعَمَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(93)\nA’MMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nFor all their deeds. \nفَاصْدَعْ بِمَا تُؤْمَرُ وَ اَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(94)\nFAASDAA’ BEMAA TUMARU WA AAA’REZ A’NIL MUSHREKEEN.\nTherefore expound openly what thou art commanded, and turn away from those who join false gods with Allah. \nاِنَّا كَفَيْنٰكَ الْمُسْتَهْزِءِيْنَۙ‏(95)\nINNAA KAFAYNAAKA AL-MUSTAHZEEENA.\nFor sufficient are We unto thee against those who scoff, \nالَّذِيْنَ يَجْعَلُوْنَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَۚ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(96)\nLAZEENA YAJ-A’LOONA LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nThose who adopt, with Allah, another god: but soon will they come to know. \nوَلَقَدْ نَعْلَمُ اَنَّكَ يَضِيْقُ صَدْرُكَ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(97)\nWA LAQAD NA’LAMO ANNAKA YAZEEQU SADRUKA BEMAA YAQOOLOONA.\nWe do indeed know how thy heart is distressed at what they say. \nفَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَكُنْ مِّنَ السّٰجِدِيْنَۙ‏(98)\nFA-SABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA WA KUN MENAL AS-SAAJEDEENA.\nBut celebrate the praises of thy Lord, and be of those who prostrate themselves in adoration. \nوَاعْبُدْ رَبَّكَ حَتّٰى يَاْتِيَكَ الْيَقِيْنُ‏(99)\nWAAA’BUD RABBAKA HATTAA YAATEEKA AL-YAQEENU.\nAnd serve thy Lord until there come unto thee the Hour that is Certain. ",
  "merits": "There are 99 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites Surah Hijr will get the reward equal to the number of Muhajireen and Ansaar (companions of the Holy Prophet [s.a.w.a.]) and this Surah should be written with saffron and then worn as a talisman by a new mother who cannot produce enough milk for her child.\nIf written and tied on one’s arm, it makes any business conducted by the wearer to be profitable and makes people like doing business with him. His sustenance thus increases. In a narration by Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) one can also put this Surah (written) inside the pocket or safe (for storing valuables)."
